# `go build ./internal/cmd/verify/` drops its binary here
/verify

# Platform test runners MkdirTemp(".", "_<platform>-<case>-") beside their own
# package, because the emitted Go has to build inside this module. An
# interrupted run skips the deferred RemoveAll, so the prefixes are ignored
# rather than the one case that happened to leak first.
#
# The leading underscore is what keeps a leaked one harmless: `go` skips a
# directory whose name starts with `_` or `.` when expanding `./...`, so the
# debris is invisible to `go vet ./...` and `go build ./...` rather than being
# compiled as part of the module. Without it a killed run left `go vet ./...`
# reporting a cgo diagnostic in generated code -- a real-looking failure with
# nothing behind it. The build inside the directory is unaffected: the runners
# set cmd.Dir and build `.`, which is a path rather than a pattern.
codegen/platform/*/_bt-*/
codegen/platform/*/_fyne-*/
codegen/platform/*/_gtk4-*/
codegen/platform/*/_optnarrow*/
/.sngl-consteval-*/
/cmd/sngl/sngl
